For a new project, don't install `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers`. Cloudflare renamed it to **`@cloudflare/vitest-plugin`** on 19 August 2026, when it reached v1. The config API is the same; only the package name changed. Ludion had no lessons on this, so the steps below come from Cloudflare's current docs.

### 1. Install
```sh
npm i -D vitest@^4.1.0 @cloudflare/vitest-plugin
```
The plugin needs **Vitest 4.1 or later**. Your Worker must use the ES modules format, and its `compatibility_date` must be `2022-10-31` or later.

### 2. `vitest.config.ts`
```ts
import { cloudflareTest } from "@cloudflare/vitest-plugin";
import { defineConfig } from "vitest/config";

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    cloudflareTest({
      wrangler: { configPath: "./wrangler.jsonc" },
      // Optional: override or extend settings from your Wrangler config
      miniflare: {
        kvNamespaces: ["TEST_NAMESPACE"],
      },
    }),
  ],
});
```
Older guides used `defineWorkersConfig` with `poolOptions.workers`. That was the Vitest 3 setup, and Vitest 4 replaced it with the `cloudflareTest()` plugin.

### 3. `test/tsconfig.json`
```jsonc
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "types": ["@cloudflare/vitest-plugin/types"] // cloudflare:test + cloudflare:workers types
  },
  "include": ["./**/*.ts", "../src/worker-configuration.d.ts"] // output of `wrangler types`
}
```
Run `npx wrangler types` to generate `worker-configuration.d.ts`.

### Notes
- **Older Vitest:** if you have to stay on the old package name, put `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` in place of `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin` in the imports and types. The config shape is the same. Version 0.12.x of the old package was the last to support Vitest 3.
- **Mocking outbound requests:** the v1 plugin dropped the built-in mocking. Cloudflare's docs now point to `msw` and `@msw/cloudflare` for this. A third-party write-up reports a peer-range mismatch: Cloudflare's install command uses `msw@^2.14.0`, while `@msw/cloudflare` wants `>=2.14.1`. I couldn't confirm that, so check the peer range before you install.
- **Migrating an existing project:** `npx @cloudflare/codemods vitest:pool-workers-to-vitest-plugin` updates the dependency, imports and test tsconfig. Add `--dry-run` to preview the changes first.

Sources:
- [Cloudflare: Write your first test](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/get-started/write-your-first-test/)
- [Cloudflare: Migrate to @cloudflare/vitest-plugin](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/migration-guides/migrate-to-vitest-plugin/)
- [Changelog: vitest-pool-workers is now vitest-plugin](https://docs-durable-objects-instance-replaced-errors.previews.developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-08-19-vitest-plugin/)
- [Cloudflare: Migrate from Vitest 3 to Vitest 4](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/migration-guides/migrate-from-vitest-3-to-vitest-4/)
- [eCorpIT: rename and msw peer dependency conflict](https://ecorpit.com/cloudflare-vitest-plugin-1-0-msw-peer-dependency-conflict-2026/)

